dios operated inside of other fitness facilities and on cruise ships.","context":"Non-Traditional Studio Locations","section":"Key Performance Indicators","block":490,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001802156-26-000095","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-07","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001802156","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1802156/000180215626000095/xpof-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac.bin","sha256":"ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac"}},{"id":"262bff4fec499f88aeddb521147635423d2903654dbb28323d9fecd2c35b865d","quote":"The number of licenses sold in the North America Region and globally reflect the cumulative number of licenses sold by us (or, outside of the North America Region, by or to our master franchisees), since inception through the date indicated. The number of licenses sold is not reduced by terminations. The number of licenses sold does not generally include license renewals or licenses issued in connection with a change in ownership of operating studios. Licenses contractually obligated to open refer to licenses sold net of opened studios and terminations. Licenses contractually obligated to be sold internationally reflect the number of licenses that master franchisees are contractually obligated to sell to franchisees to open internationally that have not yet opened as of the date indicated. The number of licenses contractually obligated to open is a useful indicator of the number of studios that may open in the future, although it is not certain that these studios will open. Management reviews the number of licenses sold and the number of licenses contractually obligated to open to help monitor and forecast studio growth, system-wide sales and revenue streams.","context":"Licenses Sold","section":"Key Performance Indicators","block":492,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001802156-26-000095","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-07","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001802156","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1802156/000180215626000095/xpof-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac.bin","sha256":"ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac"}},{"id":"994d4caa550ef832355b6b4a687f34056700899525965cf0deb88a2305fca729","quote":"As of June 30, 2026, we estimate approximately 35% of our global license obligations are over 12 months behind the applicable development schedule due to various circumstances and are currently inactive. This delay in development has resulted in delays in studio openings and may also lead to increased terminations, which could have a negative long-term impact on our business and operating results.","context":"The number of licenses sold in the North America Region and globally reflect the cumulative number of licenses sold by us (or, outside of the North America Region, by or to our master franchisees), since inception through the date indicated. The number of licenses sold is not reduced by terminations. The number of licenses sold does not generally include license renewals or licenses issued in connection with a change in ownership of operating studios. Licenses contractually obligated to open refer to licenses sold net of opened studios and terminations. Licenses contractually obligated to be sold internationally reflect the number of licenses that master franchisees are contractually obligated to sell to franchisees to open internationally that have not yet opened as of the date indicated. The number of licenses contractually obligated to open is a useful indicator of the number of studios that may open in the future, although it is not certain that these studios will open. Management reviews the number of licenses sold and the number of licenses contractually obligated to open to help monitor and forecast studio growth, system-wide sales and revenue streams.","section":"Key Performance Indicators","block":493,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001802156-26-000095","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-07","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001802156","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1802156/000180215626000095/xpof-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac.bin","sha256":"ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac"}},{"id":"70065a35f3f738c556295f57a6d2512ec06479ff5158dbb06988009d3ee7d60c","quote":"Development fee payments on future franchise licenses","context":"40","section":"Key Performance Indicators","block":495,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001802156-26-000095","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-07","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001802156","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1802156/000180215626000095/xpof-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac.bin","sha256":"ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac"}},{"id":"81cc056d9f1ee85b7cce6794c1c806d43fa0f247aff53089d4632f2a6cbee690","quote":"As part of a multi-unit agreement, franchisees purchase an initial franchise license and make nonrefundable development fee payments to reserve the right to open additional studios. The number of development fee payments on future franchise licenses sold in the North America Region reflect the number of development fee payments received by us and unused as of period end. The number of development fee payments on future franchise licenses is not included in the licenses sold count. The remaining balance of the franchise license fee for each additional studio is due upon site selection for the studio and signing of a franchise agreement by the franchisee. The number of development fee payments on future franchise licenses is a useful indicator of the number of additional licenses that may be sold in the future, although it is not certain that these development fee payments will result in a sold license. Management reviews the number of development fee payments on future franchise licenses to help monitor and forecast license sales and studio growth.","context":"Development fee payments on future franchise licenses","section":"Key Performance Indicators","block":496,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001802156-26-000095","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-07","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001802156","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1802156/000180215626000095/xpof-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac.bin","sha256":"ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac"}},{"id":"a1b9c8a856ec883edd06d257394bd030020511e0477adbc7b621cfd57748213d","quote":"AUV is calculated by dividing sales during the applicable period for all studios contributing to AUV by the number of studios contributing to AUV. All traditional studio locations in the North America Region are included in the AUV calculation, as long as they meet certain time since opening and sales criteria (as defined immediately below). In particular, AUV (LTM as of period end) and Quarterly AUV (run rate) are calculated as follows:","context":"Average Unit Volume","section":"Key Performance Indicators","block":498,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001802156-26-000095","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-07","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001802156","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1802156/000180215626000095/xpof-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac.bin","sha256":"ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac"}},{"id":"2cced48a0289af58f14954fb590fa22549485aacc9ba956ffaff5d093c462101","quote":"AUV (LTM as of period end) consists of the average sales for the trailing 12 calendar months for all traditional studio locations in the North America Region that opened at least 13 calendar months ago as of the measurement date and that have generated positive sales for each of the last 13 calendar months as of the measurement date.","context":"•","section":"Key Performance Indicators","block":500,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001802156-26-000095","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-07","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001802156","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1802156/000180215626000095/xpof-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac.bin","sha256":"ea9e7107ef0f995cddc856f11954c4ae9dd00570ef14c323bb02c437d0220eac"}},{"id":"648283f1125b76d6ab50633ab5a31dd399462b1a96ded54fc1ee9aeee9d35875","quote":"Quarterly AUV (run rate) consists of average quarterly sales for all traditional studio locations in North America that had opened at least six calendar months ago as of the beginning of the respective quarter, and that have non-zero sales in the respective quarter (including nominal or negative sales figures; the only figures excluded are exact $0 amounts in the quarter), multiplied by four.","context":"•","section":"Key Performance Indicators","block":502,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001802156-26-000095","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-07","reportDate"